    {
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Vectors and Scalars",
      "text": [
        "Scalar",
        "Vector",
        "Magnitude only (a single number)",
        "Examples: speed, temperature, mass",
        "Magnitude AND direction",
        "Examples: velocity, force, displacement",
        "Notation",
        "Component form: v = ⟨a, b⟩ = a i + b j",
        "Unit vectors: i = ⟨1, 0⟩, j = ⟨0, 1⟩",
        "Zero vector: 0 = ⟨0, 0⟩ (no magnitude, no direction)",
        "Magnitude: |v| = √(a² + b²) Direction angle: θ (CCW from +x)"
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Writing a Vector in Component Form",
      "text": [
        "Formula: v = ⟨x₂ − x₁, y₂ − y₁⟩ (terminal minus initial)",
        "Example: A(−2, 5) to B(3, −1)",
        "v = ⟨3 − (−2), −1 − 5⟩",
        "v = ⟨5, −6⟩",
        "Meaning: 5 units right, 6 units down",
        "Component form is position-independent — only the displacement matters."
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit3d/corrected/s_component_form.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "Components from |v| and θ",
      "text": [
        "Given |v| and θ",
        "vₓ = |v| cos θ",
        "vᵧ = |v| sin θ",
        "v = ⟨|v| cos θ, |v| sin θ⟩",
        "Example: |v| = 5, θ = 53.1°",
        "vₓ = 5 cos 53.1° ≈ 3",
        "vᵧ = 5 sin 53.1° ≈ 4",
        "v = ⟨3, 4⟩"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit3d/corrected/s_components_from_mag_theta.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "title": "Vector Addition & Scalar Multiplication",
      "text": [
        "Addition",
        "⟨a, b⟩ + ⟨c, d⟩ = ⟨a+c, b+d⟩",
        "Subtraction",
        "⟨a, b⟩ − ⟨c, d⟩ = ⟨a−c, b−d⟩",
        "Scalar ×",
        "k⟨a, b⟩ = ⟨ka, kb⟩",
        "u = ⟨3, −2⟩ and v = ⟨−1, 5⟩",
        "u + v = ⟨3+(−1), −2+5⟩ = ⟨2, 3⟩",
        "3u − 2v:",
        "3⟨3,−2⟩ − 2⟨−1,5⟩ = ⟨9,−6⟩ − ⟨−2,10⟩",
        "= ⟨9−(−2), −6−10⟩ = ⟨11, −16⟩"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit3d/corrected/s_vector_addition.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Magnitude and Direction",
      "text": [
        "Magnitude: |v| = √(a² + b²)",
        "Direction: θ = tan⁻¹(b / a) (adjust for quadrant)",
        "Example: v = ⟨−3, 4⟩",
        "|v| = √(9 + 16) = √25 = 5",
        "tan⁻¹(4/−3) ≈ −53.1°",
        "Q II (a < 0, b > 0): add 180°",
        "θ ≈ −53.1° + 180° = 126.9°"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit3d/corrected/s_magnitude_direction.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Direction Angle — Quadrant Adjustment",
      "text": [
        "One Rule for θ",
        "Compute α = tan⁻¹(b/a), then:",
        "if a < 0 → θ = α + 180°",
        "(Q II or Q III)",
        "else if b < 0 → θ = α + 360°",
        "(Q IV)",
        "otherwise → θ = α",
        "(Q I)"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit3d/corrected/s_quadrant_arrows.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Direction Angle of ai + bj",
      "text": [
        "Find the direction angle of v = −5i + 12j.",
        "Convert to components:",
        "v = −5i + 12j → ⟨−5, 12⟩ (a = −5, b = 12)",
        "Find magnitude:",
        "|v| = √(25 + 144) = √169 = 13",
        "Find direction:",
        "tan⁻¹(12/−5) ≈ −67.4°",
        "a < 0, b > 0 → Q II: add 180°",
        "θ ≈ −67.4° + 180° = 112.6°"
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Scalar Multiplication — Visual",
      "text": [
        "Rules",
        "|k| > 1 → stretches the vector",
        "0 < |k| < 1 → shrinks the vector",
        "k < 0 → reverses direction",
        "k⟨a, b⟩ = ⟨ka, kb⟩",
        "Magnitude: |kv| = |k| × |v|"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit3d/corrected/s_scalar_multiplication.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
